{
  "$comment": "One command source. `menus` is the native menu bar (src-tauri/src/menu.rs builds it; the custom title bar opens the same menus as popups): File (windows, folders, files, Settings…), View (the rail items in rail order, Plans, then the Explorer and the data reload), Go (go to a file, a command, the active file, back and forward), Terminal, Run, Help. `config` is the action rows of the Settings view (the top bar gear and File → Settings… show it), which holds settings only: src/main.ts renders each row under its `group` label, after the Appearance choices (Skin, Title bar, Rail) of its own markup; `omarchyOnly` rows show on Omarchy only. An id lives in exactly one of the two (menu.rs tests check it against the action map in src/main.ts, runAction), and the Commands palette lists both. No mnemonics (& or _) and no accelerators: GTK would take those keys from the terminals and the editor.",
